`]}),e.jsxs(n,{title:"One model's reason to keep RoPE",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:['Qwen3.8-Flash-Next is a hybrid model. Its Gated DeltaNet layers, a form of linear attention that Week 8 covers, alternate 3:1 with full-attention layers. For those full-attention layers, the Qwen team compared RoPE with NoPE. They report: "RoPE and a NoPE variant without positional encoding show little difference during pretraining, but the NoPE variant exhibits a substantially higher rate of endless generation after post-training" ',e.jsx(a,{id:"qwen2026qwen38flashnext",children:"Qwen Team, 2026"}),". Endless generation means the model does not stop its answer. So the full-attention layers keep RoPE. In the shipped model they are Qwen Sparse Attention layers, with RoPE on 64 dimensions."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Kazemnejad et al. found that NoPE generalizes best to longer sequences on their controlled tasks ",e.jsx(a,{id:"kazemnejad2023",children:"Kazemnejad et al., 2023"}),". Qwen measured something else: how often a post-trained model fails to stop. The two results answer different questions, so they do not contradict each other. Qwen's is one model's report."]})]})]})]}),`
